    "text": "When Maria was fourteen, she noticed that several of her classmates arrived at school without breakfast. Instead of simply complaining, she decided to do something [[1]] it. First, she persuaded a local bakery to donate bread. Then she asked her friends [[2]] they could give her a hand. Within a month, twenty volunteers were helping, and whenever Maria was busy with exams, her brother would hold the fort and make the sandwiches [[3]] that she could revise in peace.\n\nThe idea grew faster [[4]] anyone expected. Meetings were meant to finish at eight o'clock, but they often ran [[5]] by an hour because everyone had so many ideas. Soon an overwhelming majority of local residents were supporting the project. A trader at the stock exchange, [[6]] had read about her in a magazine, sent a large donation, and she was able to rent a small kitchen. Maria says she could never have managed without [[7]] help of her friends, and she hopes [[8]] her story will inspire others to start projects of their own.",
